      src/acceptance/pipeline.py#4
      src/acceptance/mutation/settings.py#0
    [missing_case] run-candidate-tests-on-throwaway-copy/execution-skipped-when-no-editable-defects
      The execution decision skips the test run whenever no defect names an editable region, even though the criterion still covers running candidate tests on the throwaway copy.
      src/acceptance/mutation/settings.py#0
      src/acceptance/pipeline.py#3
    [condition_inverted] run-candidate-tests-on-throwaway-copy/baseline-failure-stops-the-run
      A red candidate test in the control run is treated as a reason to stop instead of being set aside, which can prevent the later throwaway-copy run from happening.
